<heading>new - Start an interactive ABC run.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  new TOPIC
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Starts an interactive ABC run for the given topic. TOPIC may be an
id or a topic name. The user sees the retrieval keys A-Z and 0-9
and enters associations on a single input line; several entries
can be separated with a semicolon. Comma is ordinary content and
never splits entries.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
An entry is placed under the key character it begins with: the
first character must be an ASCII A-Z letter or a digit. A key
prefix overrides the assignment and is not part of the stored
text. Entries that do not begin with a key character are not
stored; the run view names them.
</paragraph>

<pre>
  Augustus                -&gt; A
  1945                    -&gt; 1
  4: 1945                 -&gt; 4
  a: plenty of distance   -&gt; A
</pre>

<paragraph>
Press Ctrl+N to finish the run. Finishing stores one immutable run
snapshot; an empty run is discarded. Entries under the same key
that differ only in case are stored once; the spelling of the
first entry is kept. The submitted input is cleared after each
Enter and appears only in the accumulated entries. During the run
no previous answers, suggestions, search, autocomplete, AI or
evaluation are shown. Press Esc to pause the run and Ctrl+X to
cancel it without storing anything.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
new "Roman Empire"
  Start an ABC run for the topic Roman Empire.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
list, show
</paragraph>
